<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15653" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēmissĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				sending out</i>, <i>darting forth</i> (rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i>a letting go</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radiorum ex oculis,</span>”
				<i>a darting forth</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					5, 16, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortui sunt in emissione,</span>”
				<i>in exile</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Baruch. 2, 25</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>power of
			projecting</i> or <i>hurling;</i> in
			plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">graviores telorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 2, 24, 57</span></i>
			; <i>a letting go</i>, <i>releasing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anguis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 2, 29, 62</span></i>
			 (thrice).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
